---
import DashboardLayout from '@/layouts/Dashboard.astro';
---

<DashboardLayout>
  <article class="max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl">Privacy policy</h2>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Last updated: 3 August 2026.
      This policy describes the data that VulnTrends collects about
      its visitors, how that data is used, and how to exercise your
      rights under applicable privacy laws (UK GDPR / EU GDPR /
      CCPA).
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Data VulnTrends collects</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      VulnTrends is a <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">static website</strong>.
      It has no user accounts, no forms, no comment system, no search
      backend, and no server-side storage of visitor data. The site does not
      set any first-party cookies itself by default (except for the consent cookie
      stored by Google's CMP if AdSense is enabled) and does not collect names,
      email addresses, IP addresses, or any other personal information directly.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      The data displayed on the dashboard — vulnerability records,
      advisories, CVSS scores — comes entirely from
      <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">publicly available sources</strong>
      (Mozilla MFSA, Microsoft MSRC, Google Project Zero, the National
      Vulnerability Database, and others). No non-public data is
      included; no contributor- or visitor-derived data is mixed in.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Third-party services</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Two third-party services may load when you visit VulnTrends.
      Both are opt-in via the site operator's environment configuration
      and are <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">disabled by default on
      staging deployments</strong>.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-vt-text-secondary">Plausible Analytics</h4>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Plausible is a privacy-friendly analytics service that helps us
      understand aggregate traffic patterns (page views, referrer
      sources, country). Plausible is
      <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">cookieless</strong> — it does
      not set cookies, does not collect IP addresses, and does not
      create persistent user identifiers. Aggregated counts are sent
      without any personal data, so Plausible does not require consent
      under GDPR. See
      <a
        href="https://plausible.io/data-policy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-vt-accent hover:text-vt-accent-hover underline"
      >Plausible's data policy</a
      > for details.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-vt-text-secondary">Google AdSense</h4>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Some pages — blog posts and chart click-through pages — display
      ads served by Google AdSense. The dashboard, about page, blog
      index, and privacy page are deliberately ad-free (see the
      monetisation convention in <code>AGENTS.md</code> for why). The
      AdSense script is only emitted on pages with an AdSlot, so the
      consent dialog and any ad-related cookies only appear on those
      pages.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Google AdSense uses cookies to serve ads, including — when
      consent is granted — Google's
      <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">DoubleClick (DART) cookie</strong>
      for personalisation. AdSense may also use the cookie to limit how
      often a given ad is shown and to measure ad performance.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-vt-text-secondary">Consent management</h4>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      When the AdSense script loads, Google's Consent Management
      Platform (CMP) displays a consent dialog to visitors in the EEA,
      UK, and Switzerland. If you decline, you will still see ads but
      they will be <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">non-personalised</strong>
      — they are selected based on the page content rather than your
      profile. Consent (or decline) is stored in a first-party cookie
      and respected on subsequent visits.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Visitors outside the EEA/UK/Switzerland see personalised ads by
      default; you can opt out at any time via
      <a
        href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-vt-accent hover:text-vt-accent-hover underline"
      >Google Ads Settings</a
      > or your browser's ad-blocking settings.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-vt-text-secondary">Ad technology providers</h4>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      AdSense partners with a set of ad technology providers (ATPs).
      The full list of vendors that may receive data via this site is
      maintained by Google at
      <a
        href="https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/9012903"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-vt-accent hover:text-vt-accent-hover underline"
      >Manage your ad technology partners</a
      >. You can review and exercise opt-out rights for each provider
      from that page.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Cookies</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      The only cookies set by VulnTrends itself are the consent cookie
      stored by Google's CMP after you respond to the consent dialog.
      All other cookies on pages with ads are set by Google AdSense
      (or its ATPs). The dashboard, about page, blog index, and
      privacy page set
      <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">no cookies</strong> — the
      AdSense script is never loaded there, so neither AdSense
      cookies nor the CMP consent cookie are set.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      On pages with ads (blog posts and chart pages), the AdSense
      script loads and AdSense may set cookies regardless of whether
      you consent to personalised ads. Choosing
      <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">decline</strong> in the
      consent dialog limits how those cookies are used (to non-
      personalised ads) but does not prevent them from being set.
      The only way to avoid AdSense cookies entirely is to use
      browser-level ad blocking or to not visit those pages.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Your rights</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      Under UK GDPR / EU GDPR, you have the right to:
    </p>

    <ul class="mb-4 pl-6 space-y-2 text-vt-text-secondary list-disc">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">Access</strong> any personal
        data held about you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">Erasure</strong> of personal
        data held about you ("right to be forgotten").
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">Object</strong> to processing
        for direct marketing or analytics.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">Restrict</strong> processing
        of your data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">Data portability</strong> —
        receive your data in a machine-readable format.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      In practice, <strong class="text-vt-text-primary">Plausible collects no
      personal data</strong> at all (it is a cookieless, aggregate-only
      service), and AdSense data is held by Google — see their
      <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-vt-accent hover:text-vt-accent-hover underline"
      >Privacy Policy</a
      > for the relevant access and erasure procedures.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      If you wish to exercise rights directly against VulnTrends
      (for example, to ask whether any of your data is held), use the
      contact details below. We will respond within one calendar month.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Children's privacy</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      VulnTrends is not directed at children under 13. The site does
      not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe
      a child has interacted with this site and you wish to raise a
      concern, please contact us.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Changes to this policy</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes
      (for example, enabling a new third-party service or adding a new
      category of data collection) will be noted by bumping the "Last
      updated" date at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-lg text-vt-text-secondary">Contact</h3>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      VulnTrends is a personal project run by Rob Pomeroy. For privacy
      enquiries, please open an issue on the project's
      <a
        href="https://github.com/robpomeroy/vulntrends/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-vt-accent hover:text-vt-accent-hover underline"
      >GitHub repository</a
      > or reach out via the contact details listed there.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-vt-text-secondary">
      For the operator-side guide to enabling, configuring, and
      changing the AdSense integration on this site (creating ad
      units, configuring the consent dialog, troubleshooting), see
      <a
        href="https://github.com/robpomeroy/vulntrends/blob/main/docs/monetisation.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-vt-accent hover:text-vt-accent-hover underline"
      >docs/monetisation.md</a
      > on GitHub.
    </p>
  </article>
</DashboardLayout>
